{{Wireless adapter |brand=HP |model=RSVLD-0707 |revision=(1150-7931) |fcc_date=01/25/2008 |is_manuf=No |manuf=Lite-On |manuf_model=WN4300A |if=USB (non-standard connector) |if_bus_version=2.0 |form_factor=module |vendor_id=0ace |device_id=1215 |fcc_id=B94RSVLD0707 |ic_id=466F-RSVLD0707 |chip1_brand=Atheros |chip1_model=AR2524;AR2524-AQ1C, D362Y.1J, 0728, TAIWAN; |chip2_brand=Atheros |chip2_model=AR2124;AR2124-AL1C, CR1615.01D, 0739, TAIWAN; |accessible_UART=No |ant_conn=none |802dot11_protocols=bg }} :'''HP''' P/N {{HP PN|1150-7931}}
"WN4300A V03", "TXDIVE", "323C160673B7", and "Pluto Rev 3" :is silkscreened on the board in the FCC photos. The module pin definition is in the FCC manual. {{see also|Lite-On WN4300A}} Additional specifications, per the FCC manual / datasheet.. :This adapter probably isn't supported by standard zd1211rw Linux kernel driver :(lacks support for AR2124 RFIC chip), however may be supported by this [[ZyDAS]] :Linux driver: [https://wikidevi.wi-cat.ru/files/ZyDAS/ZD1211_USB/Linux/LinuxUSB_AR2524-3.0.0.56.tgz LinuxUSB_AR2524-3.0.0.56.tgz]
*[https://alexkaltsas.wordpress.com/2014/07/22/hacking-a-printerss-wifi-module/ Hacking a Printer's Wi-Fi Module] :Notes the USB ID as the default ZD1211B ID, 0ace:1215 :Notes 3.3V supply voltage
